        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0905" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg835"/>

                <head>No. 536.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 27,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 55.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 168, of the 25th ultimo, reporting the outrage perpetrated by Armenians upon
                    the Rev. R. M. Cole, an American citizen, in the city of Erzingan, and your
                    action in immediately addressing the Turkish Government asking that the
                    offenders be punished.</p>
                <p>In approving your course as discreet and prompt, I have to add that it is hoped
                    the result will be immediate and satisfactory.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
